mission "The Observatory's Blue Flame"
    name "The Observatory's Blue Flame"
    description "Carry the brass token to the island observatory; its old instruments may explain the blue lights."
    source "San Aurelio"
    destination "Bellweather Cay"
    reward 745
    speaker offer "Keeper Orlan"
    speaker visit "Keeper Orlan"
    speaker complete "Keeper Orlan"
    to offer
        has "A Chart Beneath the Bell: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The observatory's brass instruments are laid out beneath a shuttered window. The blue lights have been seen again, and Keeper Orlan has set the recovered token beside the old sighting records.`
            `Keeper Orlan turns the token toward the lamplight. "This may belong to the expedition that vanished west. The observatory keeps instruments older than the Company, and they may tell us whether those blue lights were signal, warning, or something else."`
            choice
                `"All right. Put me on the course."`
                    accept
                `"Why has someone gone to such trouble to hide this?"`
                    goto details
                `"My ship has enough trouble without this. I will pass."`
                    close
            label details
                `Orlan taps the old sighting book. "I have tried to make these instruments agree with the modern charts. They do not. Bring the token here, and we may learn why the expedition's route was left blank."`
                choice
                    `"Mark the course. My ship is ready."`
                        accept
                    `"Not this voyage. Find another ship."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Observatory's Blue Flame. Carry the brass token to the island observatory; its old instruments may explain the blue lights."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Bellweather Cay, Orlan fits the token against a worn brass mount. The old instruments point toward a place missing from modern charts. "They were not looking for gold alone," Orlan says. "Someone removed the destination from every official record."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Orlan closes the shutters over the instruments. "The blue flame has given us a direction, not an answer. Still, a direction is more than we had yesterday. Let us keep the finding in the hands of those who live here."`
        log "Completed The Observatory's Blue Flame. Received 745 gold. Carry the brass token to the island observatory; its old instruments may explain the blue lights."
